# Codebase Engineer — backend environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the `backend/` directory and fill in only the
# values you actually need. Every variable here is optional — the server
# runs with sane defaults and no `.env` file at all. This file is loaded
# automatically on startup via `dotenv/config` (see src/server.ts); nothing
# else needs to change. `.env` itself is gitignored, so real secrets never
# get committed.

# --- Core server (all optional, sane defaults shown) -----------------------

# PORT=4000
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# Where the SQLite database and other app data live. Defaults to
# ~/.codebase-engineer if unset.
# CODEBASE_ENGINEER_DATA_DIR=

# Only needed if serving the built frontend from somewhere other than the
# default location baked in by `npm run build` (see docs/PACKAGING.md).
# CODEBASE_ENGINEER_STATIC_DIR=

# Set to 1/true ONLY once this process sits behind a reverse proxy you
# control that terminates TLS (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md's "Going live behind
# a reverse proxy" section). This is what lets the auth session cookie's
# `secure` flag correctly turn on in that setup, by trusting the proxy's
# X-Forwarded-Proto/X-Forwarded-For headers. Leave unset for local dev or
# any setup where this process is reached directly — trusting those
# headers from an untrusted client would let them spoof its protocol/IP.
# TRUST_PROXY=

# --- AI providers ------------------------------------------------------
#
# Not configured here. AI provider keys (OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic,
# etc.) are entered and stored in the app's own database via the AI Mode
# settings page in the UI, not as environment variables — see
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 and docs/AI_MODE.md.

# --- Billing (Razorpay) — fully optional, see docs/MONETIZATION.md §6 ------
#
# Leave all three of these unset (the default) and billing stays entirely
# off: AI Mode usage is unlimited, and the Settings/Billing page just shows
# "Billing is not configured on this server." Nothing else in the app
# changes or degrades.
#
# Provider: Dodo Payments (https://dodopayments.com) — a merchant-of-
# record platform for AI/SaaS products, chosen after Razorpay's merchant
# onboarding rejected this product's live account application (self-
# hosted software falls under their restricted "hosting" category).
#
# Set all three together to turn billing on:
#
# DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
# DODO_PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_KEY=whsec_your_webhook_signing_secret_here
# DODO_PRODUCT_ID=your_pro_subscription_product_id_here
#
# Optional, only relevant once billing is on:
#
# DODO_PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT=test_mode    # test_mode (default) or live_mode — picks the matching API base URL below unless DODO_API_BASE_URL overrides it.
# DODO_API_BASE_URL=https://test.dodopayments.com   # Override only for testing against a mock; normally derived from DODO_PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT.
# DODO_RETURN_URL=/settings              # Where Dodo's hosted checkout redirects after payment. A relative path resolves against this server's own origin; default shown.

# --- Auth (local accounts + OAuth + Turnstile) — fully optional, see docs/AUTH.md ------
#
# Local email/password register+login works with ZERO variables set below —
# it's always available. The instance stays in "open" mode (no login wall
# at all, today's behavior) until the first account is actually
# registered; only then does every route start requiring a session. See
# docs/AUTH.md for the full setup guide, including exactly how to create
# the Google/GitHub OAuth apps and the Turnstile widget.

# Required once you enable Google or GitHub OAuth (Task #82/#83) — used to
# encrypt the GitHub access token at rest (it can read your private repos)
# and any Google refresh token. Generate a real random value, e.g.
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. Do NOT reuse this example value.
# AUTH_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=change-me-to-a-real-random-64-char-hex-string

# Google OAuth (sign-in, and Drive access for the Drive zip picker) — from
# a Google Cloud Console OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application type).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/google/callback

# GitHub OAuth (sign-in + repo browsing) — from a GitHub OAuth App
# (Settings -> Developer settings -> OAuth Apps).
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GITHUB_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/github/callback

# Cloudflare Turnstile (bot protection on the register/login forms) — the
# secret key stays server-side. The matching site key is a frontend env
# var (VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY, in frontend/.env — it's meant to be public,
# unlike everything else on this page).
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
